<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perdiccas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 321 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Perdiccas was a Macedonian general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> who became regent of the empire after Alexander's death in 323 BCE. In 322 BCE he conquered Cappadocia, executing its ruler Ariarathes, to install Eumenes there. His ambitions turned the other generals against him, and during a failed invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> against Ptolemy his own officers murdered him in 321 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/perdiccas.jpg" alt="Perdiccas" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philip_III_Arrhidaios_Babylon_mint_struck_under_Perdikkas_circa_323_320_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
